  "summary": "Opened {{v5}}, clicked Edit, then Dashboard settings > General and entered the tag 'bench' in the Tags field (chip 'Remove \"bench\" tag' rendered, confirming the tag was accepted). Set the top-bar time picker to 'Last 6 hours', then used Save dashboard, ticked the 'Update default time range' checkbox in the save drawer and confirmed — the page reported the 'Dashboard saved' alert/status and the drawer closed. I exited edit mode and reloaded the page fresh (plain dashboard URL); the live DOM then showed the breadcrumb '{{v4}} Bench Dashboard' and the time picker still reading 'Last 6 hours' (URL from=now-6h), and the save drawer reopened with Save disabled and 'No changes to save', so everything was persisted. Both panels remain: '{{v4}} Notes' (Text, rendering 'Bench notes for run {{v4}}') and '{{v4}} Availability' (Stat, TestData). One thing I could not re-confirm: after the fresh reload I ran out of turns before re-opening Dashboard settings to see the 'bench' tag on the reloaded page (it is not shown in the breadcrumb); the tag and its inclusion in the successful save were observed on the live page immediately before saving.",
